p.src:
At fixed $L$, radial equilibrium requires a stationary point: $\frac{d}{dr}
\left[
\frac{\sqrt{1-\frac{2MG}{r}}}{r}
\right]=0.$ Differentiating, $-\frac{\sqrt{1-\frac{2MG}{r}}}{r^{2}}
+
\frac{MG}
{r^{3}\sqrt{1-\frac{2MG}{r}}}
=0,$ and hence $r=3MG.$ This radius is one and a half times the Schwarzschild radius. It is usually called the photon sphere.

